{"activity_text": "Antifungal, candidacidal, anti-sepsis", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (92%) to Hp1090. The peptide sequence from Octopus minor corresponds to N-terminal FF truncated form of chrysophsin-2 from Chrysophrys major. Activity: Weakly active against C. albicans (MIC 50 ug/mL), which was essentially all killed at 100 ug/ml (MFC). Also showed significant activity against carbapenem-resistant E. coli (MIC 4-8 ug/ml) MBC higher (see the 2023 Kong ref). In vitro Toxicity: weak toxicity to RAW 264.7 cell line till 128 ug/ml (toxic at 256 ug/ml); likewise, little hemo.lytic at 128 ug/ml (increased toxicity at 256 ug/ml or greater). MOA:fungi: It appears to act on membranes and may also induce ROS release. 95% HEK293T cells survived at 100 ug/ml. Animal model:zebrafish: showed in vivo efficacy; Animal model:wax moth: it also protected G. mellonella from infection-caused death ( Kong et al., 2023. Updated 9/2023", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "31952292", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mar Drugs. 2020 Jan 15;18(1):56. doi: 10.3390/md18010056. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03250", "source_id": "AP03250", "source_numeric_id": "03250", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03250", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Octominin: A Novel Synthetic Anticandidal Peptide Derived from Defense Protein of Octopus minor", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
